<p class="lead"><strong>Thank you to everyone who completed the recent survey, shared evidence or volunteered.</strong> The results show a range of views. The clearest priority was to prepare for a possible legal route, while continuing to build evidence, give owners a public voice and test whether JLR's individual-case approach produces lasting outcomes.</p>

<p><a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/updates/october-2026-member-priorities/">See the published October survey results</a></p>

<h2>Legal preparation and coordination</h2>

<p>We are coordinating legal preparation in the UK, with local leads joining as other regions come on line. Tim is helping lead this work alongside new volunteers. It is preparation, not a claim: any representation, proceedings or costs would need separate, explicit authority from eligible members.</p>

<p>Please make sure your <a href="/member/account/">legal name and formal contact address are recorded privately in My Data</a>. That helps avoid delay if members later choose to take a defined next step. Registering your details does not commit you to any legal action, but is a prerequisite for any future legal process.</p>

<h2>More member stories, wider reach</h2>

<p>Our reach is growing on several fronts. Ole is leading our Northern Europe efforts from Norway, and Kevin is leading Southern Europe from France. Kevin, a long-time contributor, to <a href="https://www.ipaceforums.co.uk/f">I-PACE Forums</a>, also brings valuable experience and connections. Thank you both for joining the core team, and to the other volunteers who continue to support our efforts.</p>

<p>We have built a member-stories feature so owners can prepare an account of their experience with photos or video. With separate publication permission, a story can help our website, social channels and press packs. It is in final testing: <a href="/member/account/">register interest in trying new member features</a> if you would like to help test this or other features before wider release.</p>

<h2>Evidence: Improved document imports next</h2>

<p>We are working on a secure in-browser way to import service information and documents into your private record. It is still in development, but the aim is simple: make it easier to retain the facts that matter without emailing sensitive documents around.</p>

<p>In the meantime, and in preparation, please check your <a href="/member/dashboard/">vehicle(s) are registered and submit your Executive Office Response</a> experience if you contacted JLR directly.</p>

<h2>The unanswered battery question</h2>

<p>JLR says cases will be considered individually, including warranty or goodwill factors. So far, the outcomes we have seen do not provide a clear precedent for modules failing outside the high-voltage warranty due to the known manufacturing issues.</p>

<p><b>The question is simple:</b> If a module fails outside the high-voltage warranty, is it treated as a safety concern or as chargeable degradation?</p>

<p>Diagnostics messages shown to owners must establish the cause clearly. With diagnosis and replacement potentially costing hundreds or thousands of pounds, that distinction matters. H572 is still unannounced, although rumoured to be landing soon, so its scope and what it means for future module failures remain unknown.</p>

<h2>Keep building the case</h2>

<p>We appreciate your ongoing contributions. Please keep recording service outcomes and costs, recruiting other owners, and volunteering skills where you can. We will continue to monitor developments and share updates as they become available. Stronger together.</p>

